Notification delivery exceptions were silently ignored due to using `thenRunAsync`. This replaces it with `whenCompleteAsync` to capture and log exceptions.


**Modified:** `PublishingManager.onPublishComplete()`
- Changed `callback.thenRunAsync()` → `callback.whenCompleteAsync()`
- Added exception check with warning log before processing completion

// Before: exceptions ignored
callback.thenRunAsync(() -> {
    pendingCount.getAndUpdate(p -> (p > 0) ? p - 1 : 0);
    maybeSendPublishRequests();
}, executor);

// After: exceptions logged
callback.whenCompleteAsync((unit, ex) -> {
    if (ex != null) {
        logger.warn("Notification delivery threw an unexpected Exception: {}", ex.getMessage(), ex);
    pendingCount.getAndUpdate(p -> (p > 0) ? p - 1 : 0);
    maybeSendPublishRequests();
}, executor);

The backpressure mechanism remains unchanged—publish requests still wait for notification delivery to complete before sending more requests.

